3/3 Cybertrucks, Twins and Tesla Life Worldwide
Wednesday, November 18, 2026

@CyberDadx2: This is not a mirror: his Cybertruck met a Florida twin with the same white wrap, the same pillar delete and an owner with the same first name. What are the odds? Find the video on their X page.

@drmarkmancini: Polishing day on the Cyberbeast: the stainless gets so shiny you end up staring at your own reflection mid buff. Find the photo on their X page.

@drvrjay: The Cybertruck RC Racer has arrived. The only question left: read the directions, or just send it? Find the photo on their X page.

@CranzillaX: Bart Simpson offers to wash the Cybertruck for five bucks and shotgun on the next Supercharger run. Ay caramba, it is shiny. Find the video on their X page.

@Mohammadsuwaidi: From the UAE: people say the Cybertruck looks like it is from another planet, so he took it to the mountains of Ras Al Khaimah to find its natural habitat. Even the rocks are less angular. Find the photos on their X page.

@SkyXFunNext: That white Model Y looks so fresh that even the Ram parked next to it wants a kiss. Find the video on their X page.

@CKEVS1998: Cold weather is here, the tire pressure keeps dropping, and the air pump is now a weekly appointment. Tesla fam, is it just them? Find the photo on their X page.

@geeksobreruedas: Waiting on GTA 6 got out of hand, so the Model 3 got a full Vice City skin with its own name on the door. Find the video on their X page.

@TeslaHistorian: A 2017 headline promised Model 3 buyers would flee faster than electrons. It went on to become one of the best selling EVs in the world. Find the photo on their X page.

Sources: @CyberDadx2, @drmarkmancini, @drvrjay, @CranzillaX, @Mohammadsuwaidi, @SkyXFunNext, @CKEVS1998, @geeksobreruedas, @TeslaHistorian. Picture: Wikimedia Commons photoreal photo.

